+# LanguageStandard/ManualProcessorCompilation affect the command line that the
+# ninja generator builds too, so they are declared as real flags rather than
+# MSBuild-only.  msvs_emulation.py emits "/std:<lang>" for them and filters /MP
+# back out (ninja does its own parallel scheduling), but declaring them here is
+# what stops the "unrecognized setting" warning from drowning the build log.
+_Same(
